      "content": "I can help you write a script to bypass the standard RPC layers and extract the raw, unindexed data from the local database. You can use the `leveldb` command-line tool to achieve this. \n\nHere's a basic script to get you started:\n\n```bash\n# Get the raw, unindexed hex values for the first several hundred block headers\nleveldb --debug --path=/path/to/leveldb/db --format=raw < /path/to/leveldb/db/0\n\n# Extract the raw bytes from the block headers\nfor i in {0..499}; do\n  block_header=$(leveldb --debug --path=/path/to/leveldb/db --format=raw \"get /blocks/0/${i}\" | cut -d' ' -f2-)\n  echo \"Block ${i}: ${block_header}\"\ndone\n```\n\nThis script will extract the raw block headers from the local database, without any middleware or client-side interpretation. You can then compare the extracted bytes with your original implementation files to prove the sequence is yours.\n\nNote: Make sure to replace `/path/to/leveldb/db` with the actual path to your local database. Also, be aware",
